adjudication.rationale:
In packages/core/EventManager.ts the diff introduces:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null`/`undefined` or an empty array (`[]`), destructuring yields `mainHostDestinationCalendar === undefined`. When `evt.location === MeetLocationType` is true, the RHS of `&&` is evaluated and `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` throws a TypeError (cannot read properties of undefined). The diff elsewhere explicitly starts producing `destinationCalendar: []` when missing, making this scenario plausible and verifiable from the changes shown.
